  "caption": "Quinn's cold finally cleared, so naturally Quinn went straight back to full-speed runs. Ten minutes later: jelly legs.\n\nAfter an illness, the body is often still catching up, and jumping back to your old training load is a common cause of relapse or injury.\n\nWhat often helps: rest if symptoms are in the chest or you have a fever or body aches, wait 24–48 hours after a fever, start almost too easy, then step up in stages, holding each for a day or two. Light strength work can often come back early at a lower load.\n\nChest pain, a racing heart, dizziness or fatigue that crashes for days after activity means stopping and checking in with your GP.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
